      "question": {
        ":question/id": "1025e586-56eb-5f51-a7a1-dc54947df174",
        ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 10 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 5 & -6 & -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-24 & 0 & -21 \\\\ 10 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 35 & 0 & 26\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form $R_{i}:=R_{i}+kR_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?",
        ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above and below $a_{22}=2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 10 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 5 & -6 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{1}:=R_{1}-3R_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}-24 & 0 & -21 \\\\ 10 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 5 & -6 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{3}:=R_{3}+3R_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}-24 & 0 & -21 \\\\ 10 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 35 & 0 & 26\\end{bmatrix}=B\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$R_{1}:=R_{1}-3R_{2}$ and $R_{3}:=R_{3}+3R_{2}$.",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
